      "image": null,
      "content": "Most evaluations of AI coding agents rely on anecdotal impressions rather than controlled experimentation. The Context Engine Simulator introduces a repeatable way to measure whether pre-gathered organizational context actually helps agents complete tasks faster and cheaper.\n\nThe framework executes an A/B test in two isolated git worktrees simultaneously. The baseline arm proceeds straight from task description to planning, review, and implementation. Meanwhile, the context-enhanced arm gathers workspace context and architectural patterns before running a context-aware planning phase.\n\nBoth outputs are scored against explicit acceptance criteria across CLIs like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor. This lets engineering teams measure the exact delta in token cost, execution time, and task pass rate caused by their context enrichment layer.\n\nSystematic benchmarking is the only reliable way to prevent context bloat from degrading agent performance."
