      "image": null,
      "content": "Hooking an LLM agent directly into Slack, Jira, and GitHub via Model Context Protocol connectors gives it direct access to your tools, but access is not the same as context. Point-to-point connectors map one-to-one to underlying search APIs, returning fragmented document lists that leave the agent to cross-reference data and resolve contradictions at inference time.\n\nRunning cross-tool synthesis inside the agent loop burns context windows fast. Benchmarks demonstrate that pre-assembling connected metadata into a dedicated context engine before the model queries it yields up to 83 percent faster task completion while cutting token consumption down to roughly 40 percent of baseline tool-calling runs.\n\nWhen agents must trace historical decisions spread across old pull request reviews, ephemeral chat threads, and incident postmortems, fetching raw hits individually turns tool calling into a latency bottleneck. Context resolution belongs in the retrieval pipeline, not the reasoning loop."
